    "plain_text": "Alexander W. Dreyfoos Jr. was an American engineer, inventor and philanthropist who founded Photo Electronics Corporation. His colour-imaging systems earned an Academy Award and multiple patents, while sales of his technology and television interests financed extensive support for arts, education and neuroscience. He helped establish Palm Beach County’s cultural council, performing-arts centre and arts school.",
